  "term": "flute",
  "says": "Reid's flute: a nearly pure tone (a sine or a soft triangle - the flute's spectrum is the fundamental and a weak second harmonic) with breath noise mixed under it, an attack of 50-150 ms (the air column takes time), a vibrato around 5 Hz, and the noise louder at the onset than in the sustain. Signature: harmonic, a centroid close to the fundamental, a soft attack, a little noise in the spectrum (flatness above a sine's zero), narrow.",
